Package Update Test Suite

Package Update Test Suite is framework for testing of package install/update.
This test suite verifies whether PackageManagerService can manage installed applications and
user data correctly through SW update (ROM1 -> ROM2).

Background:
- PackageManagerService is huge and complicated.
- Bugs in PackageManagerService cause serious problems on market.
- To maintain PackageManagerService securely, automated test is thought to be needed.

How to use it:

[Prerequisite]
- Ubuntu PC is required.
  - Test execution has been verified on Ubuntu14.
  - Add udev rule into /etc/udev/rules.d/51-android.rules for detecting target device by fastboot.
    see: https://developer.android.com/studio/run/device.html
- Pixel / Pixel 2 are available with bootloader unlocked fully.
- Latest fastboot
- Download ROM images
  Need to place 2 version ROM for simulating letter update
  ex:ROM
      + -- radio.img
      + -- bootloader.img
      + -- aosp_walleye-img-xxxx-zip
- Build Android code
    - see: https://source.android.com/setup/build/building

[Run test]
 1. Move to root directory of source tree
 2. $ source ./build/envsetup.sh
 3. $ lunch <device-target>
 4. Create test applications
    $ make package_update_testapps
    NOTE:
      Build test applications and create zip archive in
        $OUT/obj/PACKAGING/PackageUpdate_intermediates/testapps/testapps.zip

 5. $ make package_update_harnesses
 6. Copy sources under frameworks/base/tests/PackageUpdate/harnesses/tradefed/ to tools/tradefederation/contrib.
    $ mkdir -p tools/tradefederation/contrib/res/config/pkgup
    $ cp frameworks/base/tests/PackageUpdate/harnesses/tradefed/config/* tools/tradefederation/contrib/res/config/pkgup/
    $ mkdir -p tools/tradefederation/contrib/src/com/android/tests/pkgup
    $ cp frameworks/base/tests/PackageUpdate/harnesses/tradefed/src/com/android/tests/pkgup/* tools/tradefederation/contrib/src/com/android/tests/pkgup/
 7. $ make tradefed-all
 8. $ tradefed.sh
 9. tf >run pkgup/<config> --rom1-zip <path/to/the/rom_1st> --rom2-zip <path/to/the/rom_2nd>

    <config> is a tradefed test configuration which has a name like basic-scope-v2s-o2p.
      - basic scope
        Testcase that is used for this configuration. Currently this framework support following 2 testcases.
        - testcases/01_basic-scope/TestcaseSpec.txt
        - testcases/02_disable-app/TestcaseSpec.txt
      - v2s
        It means test applications will be pre-installed into vendor partition at ROM1,
        and they will be pre-installed system partition at ROM2.
      - o2p
        It means that ROM1 is based on Android O, and ROM2 is based on Android P.
        It is used for evaluation of test results.

    You can get all available configurations by
      tf >list config
    command on tradefed.


[Test result]
- When all tests are executed, logs and results are placed in $OUT/obj/PACKAGING/PackageUpdate_intermediates/0/<config>/inv_<integer value>/.
    - Test summary is included in test_result_<hash>.zip.
- The detailed test results are reported in $OUT/obj/PACKAGING/PackageUpdate_intermediates/0/<config>/inv_<hash>/reports/html/analysis.html.


[Standalone package]
- Create standalone package
  1. Move to root directory of source tree
  2. $ source ./build/envsetup.sh
  3. $ lunch <device-target>
  4. Copy sources under frameworks/base/tests/PackageUpdate/harnesses/tradefed/ to tools/tradefederation/contrib.
     $ mkdir -p tools/tradefederation/contrib/res/config/pkgup
     $ cp frameworks/base/tests/PackageUpdate/harnesses/tradefed/config/* tools/tradefederation/contrib/res/config/pkgup/
     $ mkdir -p tools/tradefederation/contrib/src/com/android/tests/pkgup
     $ cp frameworks/base/tests/PackageUpdate/harnesses/tradefed/src/com/android/tests/pkgup/* tools/tradefederation/contrib/src/com/android/tests/pkgup/

  5. $ make package_update_zip
     NOTE:
       Create zip package in
         $OUT/obj/PACKAGING/PackageUpdate_intermediates/PackageUpdate.zip

- Run test
  1. $ unzip PackageUpdate.zip
  2. $ ./PackageUpdate/pkgup_tradefed run pkgup/<config> --rom1-zip <path/to/the/rom_1st> --rom2-zip <path/to/the/rom_2nd>


[Cleanup]
- If you want to reset the test environment, please execute folloing command.
    - $ make package_update_clean

